WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.128
Module four. How the admin builds the product catalog.

2
00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:09.973
Remember the golden rule: only the admin creates products.

3
00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:12.797
So this module shows exactly how that's done.

4
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:15.679
First, the catalog page and its columns.

5
00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.052
Then bulk upload using the CSV template.

6
00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:20.995
How to read upload errors.

7
00:00:21.445 --> 00:00:23.834
Adding a single product, field by field.

8
00:00:24.284 --> 00:00:27.335
And finally GST, commission and bulk pricing.

9
00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:35.023
Open Catalog in the admin panel. At the top you'll see total products, pending,

10
00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:38.839
Verified and empty products. Below is the products table.

11
00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:40.848
Here's what each column means.

12
00:00:41.298 --> 00:00:46.354
The SKU code is generated automatically, next to the product name and photo.

13
00:00:46.804 --> 00:00:50.878
Category and brand decide where the product is listed and who makes it.

14
00:00:51.328 --> 00:00:56.427
HSN and GST percent are the tax classification and the tax rate.

15
00:00:56.877 --> 00:00:59.181
Commission percent is Oribrix's share.

16
00:00:59.631 --> 00:01:04.154
MRP is the printed price, and selling price is what the customer pays.

17
00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:08.785
Status shows if it's active, and Tally shows whether it's synced to accounting.

18
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.035
There are two ways to add products.

19
00:01:13.485 --> 00:01:18.866
Bulk upload. Download the standard template, fill one row per product with photo

20
00:01:18.866 --> 00:01:24.045
Links, then drop the CSV file and upload. Use this for many products at once.

21
00:01:24.495 --> 00:01:27.624
Or a single product, using the Add product form.

22
00:01:27.624 --> 00:01:30.361
This is best for one-off or special items.

23
00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:36.074
Before you upload, know the rules of the CSV template.

24
00:01:36.524 --> 00:01:40.684
Always start from the downloaded template. Don't make your own column names.

25
00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:46.260
Four fields are mandatory for every row: product name, category name, brand name,

26
00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:46.830
And unit.

27
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.098
Photo links must be public URLs that open in a browser.

28
00:01:51.548 --> 00:01:56.303
Tick auto-create missing subcategories and brands, so new brands are created for

29
00:01:56.303 --> 00:01:56.540
You.

30
00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:02.606
And keep files small. In the demo, a big file was rejected as too large, so split

31
00:02:02.606 --> 00:02:03.369
Long lists.

32
00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.687
Let's watch this in the live demo.

33
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.988
This is the catalog page. Thirty seven products are verified, and there are buttons

34
00:02:15.988 --> 00:02:20.001
For Add product, Bulk upload, Category requests and Tally sync.

35
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.695
Every product here came from a bulk upload. Bulk upload opens a window.

36
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:57.350
Step one, download the standard template. Step two, choose your CSV file.

37
00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:59.703
Below are the required guidelines.

38
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.620
Let's watch this in the live demo.

39
00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:26.680
The file is uploaded. The result shows two boxes: products created successfully, and

40
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.782
Rows with errors.

41
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:44.221
The error details are specific. Row three, ACC Gold Water Shield cement, already

42
00:03:44.221 --> 00:03:46.982
Exists in the catalog, so it was skipped.

43
00:04:01.233 --> 00:04:03.729
The new products now appear at the top of the list.

44
00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:18.507
In the next try, the upload failed because the unit column was missing from the

45
00:04:18.507 --> 00:04:18.790
File.

46
00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:26.150
So what do the errors mean, and what should you do?

47
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.665
Already exists means a product with the same name is in the catalog.

48
00:04:30.665 --> 00:04:33.534
That row is skipped, so there are no duplicates.

49
00:04:33.984 --> 00:04:38.080
For an existing product, only its stock related data is updated.

50
00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.623
If unit is missing, fix the file and upload again.

51
00:04:42.073 --> 00:04:46.809
If a category doesn't exist, create the category first, with its image, then upload.

52
00:04:47.259 --> 00:04:50.544
And if the file is too large, split it into smaller files.

53
00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:54.853
Let's watch this in the live demo.

54
00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:03.733
Here is a bigger upload. Many products were created, and the auto-created masters

55
00:05:03.733 --> 00:05:06.923
Box lists the new brands and subcategories it made.

56
00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:21.453
The error list shows rows that already exist, and rows whose category doesn't exist

57
00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:24.139
Yet. Those need the category created first.

58
00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:39.214
Now, adding a single product. Click Add product.

59
00:05:39.214 --> 00:05:40.811
Here are the basic fields.

60
00:05:41.261 --> 00:05:47.274
The name. Make it clear and specific, with brand, grade and size, like UltraTech OPC

61
00:05:47.274 --> 00:05:49.922
Fifty three grade cement, fifty kilo.

62
00:05:50.372 --> 00:05:52.378
The category and sub category.

63
00:05:52.828 --> 00:05:56.326
The brand. Pick it from the list, or add a new brand right there.

64
00:05:56.776 --> 00:06:02.152
The unit, such as piece, bag, kilogram or box. This is how the customer will buy it.

65
00:06:02.602 --> 00:06:07.709
And the unit weight per quantity. This matters for delivery, because heavy orders go

66
00:06:07.709 --> 00:06:08.256
By cargo.

67
00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:12.587
Let's watch this in the live demo.

68
00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.228
Add product is clicked, and a form opens. The example product is House solar

69
00:06:21.228 --> 00:06:22.117
Installations.

70
00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:49.404
The category list opens. Roofing, safety equipment, steel, tiles, tools.

71
00:06:49.404 --> 00:06:50.864
Electrical is chosen.

72
00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:17.563
A sub category can be edited right here. Solar is selected as the sub category.

73
00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:40.066
The brand isn't in the list yet, so Add brand opens.

74
00:07:40.066 --> 00:07:44.720
You can see existing brands like 3M, ACC, Ambuja and Asian Paints.

75
00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.327
The new brand is added, and the unit is set to piece, because a solar installation

76
00:08:09.327 --> 00:08:10.949
Can't be measured in kilos.

77
00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.987
Then unit weight per quantity. Here, one unit weighs around eighty kilos.

78
00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.547
Next come size, tax and commission.

79
00:08:39.997 --> 00:08:44.029
Length, breadth and height in centimetres, used for packing and delivery.

80
00:08:44.479 --> 00:08:48.468
The HSN code, which is the tax classification of the product.

81
00:08:48.918 --> 00:08:51.115
Commission percent, Oribrix's share.

82
00:08:51.565 --> 00:08:53.464
GST on commission percent.

83
00:08:53.914 --> 00:09:00.139
And the pricing block: MRP, final price, GST percent, and whether the price is

84
00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.533
Inclusive or exclusive of GST.

85
00:09:04.933 --> 00:09:06.853
Let's watch this in the live demo.

86
00:09:10.667 --> 00:09:13.504
Length and breadth are filled in. Height is optional.

87
00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:32.918
Then the HSN code, and the commission. The demo used test values only.

88
00:09:48.267 --> 00:09:53.664
Here is the pricing and tax configuration. The Inclusive of GST box is ticked.

89
00:10:08.267 --> 00:10:14.010
MRP is one hundred, the final price is one hundred, and with ten percent GST, the

90
00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:18.123
System calculates the base price as ninety point nine one.

91
00:10:29.067 --> 00:10:34.691
Let's make inclusive and exclusive crystal clear, using the demo's numbers.

92
00:10:34.691 --> 00:10:40.840
The demo used ten percent GST only as a test. Always use the real GST rate for the

93
00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:41.440
Product.

94
00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:45.437
Inclusive means the price already includes GST.

95
00:10:45.437 --> 00:10:51.700
The customer pays one hundred. Inside that, ninety point nine one is the base price

96
00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:54.114
And nine point zero nine is GST.

97
00:10:54.564 --> 00:11:00.324
Exclusive means GST is added on top. A base of one hundred becomes one hundred and

98
00:11:00.324 --> 00:11:05.380
Ten at ten percent. Pick the wrong one, and the customer price is wrong.

99
00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:09.687
Let's watch this in the live demo.

100
00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:17.660
Now the description, thumbnail, images, warranty and return policy.

101
00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:36.711
A red message says GST percent is required. The form won't save until it's filled.

102
00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:55.052
The product is created. The view shows every detail: category, brand, HSN, GST,

103
00:11:55.052 --> 00:11:59.153
Commission, MRP, price type, unit and package size.

104
00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:16.178
Bulk pricing opens. Ten units at eighty five rupees each, and fifteen units at

105
00:12:16.178 --> 00:12:18.652
Eighty rupees each. Then Save pricing.

106
00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:48.548
Bulk pricing rewards bigger orders. Construction customers often buy in bulk, so

107
00:12:48.548 --> 00:12:49.841
This matters a lot.

108
00:12:50.291 --> 00:12:53.534
Up to nine units, the normal price, one hundred rupees.

109
00:12:53.984 --> 00:12:56.053
Ten or more, eighty five rupees each.

110
00:12:56.503 --> 00:13:00.962
Fifteen or more, eighty rupees each. You can add more tiers with Add tier.

111
00:13:03.367 --> 00:13:07.015
Watch out for these mistakes. They directly affect customers.

112
00:13:07.465 --> 00:13:12.222
Vague names, like just cement bag. Customers need brand, grade and size.

113
00:13:12.672 --> 00:13:16.491
The wrong GST rate, or inclusive and exclusive mixed up.

114
00:13:16.941 --> 00:13:19.480
The wrong unit, like kilo instead of bag.

115
00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:23.279
Missing unit weight, so the delivery mode is chosen wrongly.

116
00:13:23.729 --> 00:13:28.294
And broken photo links. Always open a few products after upload to check.

117
00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.329
Quick check. Your CSV upload fails with an error about unit.

118
00:13:34.329 --> 00:13:35.479
What should you do?

119
00:13:39.429 --> 00:13:44.322
Add the unit column to the CSV, fill it for every row, and upload again.

120
00:13:44.322 --> 00:13:47.109
Unit is one of the four mandatory fields.

121
00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.393
Let's sum up module four.

122
00:13:51.843 --> 00:13:56.238
Only the admin creates products, by bulk CSV or one by one.

123
00:13:56.688 --> 00:14:02.171
For CSV, use the template, fill the four mandatory fields, and keep files small.

124
00:14:02.621 --> 00:14:07.143
Read the errors. Duplicates are skipped, and categories must exist first.

125
00:14:07.593 --> 00:14:11.241
Get GST right: the rate, and inclusive or exclusive.

126
00:14:11.691 --> 00:14:16.717
And use bulk pricing tiers for big orders. Next, we'll see how vendors turn these

127
00:14:16.717 --> 00:14:18.454
Products into live listings.

128
00:14:20.867 --> 00:14:25.646
That's the end of module 4. Next up, module 5: Vendor: adding stock.
